{"name":"Glossy Kiss","hex":"#eee3de","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glossy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a smooth, silklike, reflective (shiny) surface.","Attention-grabbing and superficially attractive."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A glossy magazine.","A glossy photograph."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glossy"},{"term":"kiss","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To touch with the lips or press the lips against, usually to show love or affection or passion, or as part of a greeting.","To (cause to) touch lightly or slightly; to come into contact."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A touch with the lips, usually to express love or affection, or as a greeting.","An 'X' mark placed at the end of a letter or other type of message, signifying the bestowal of a kiss from the sender to the receiver."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/kiss"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gloss (optics)","blocks":[{"text":"Gloss is an optical property which indicates how well a surface reflects light in a specular (mirror-like) direction. It is one of the important parameters that are used to describe the visual appearance of an object. Other categories of visual appearance related to the perception of regular or diffuse reflection and transmission of light have been organized under the concept of cesia in an order system with three variables, including gloss among the involved aspects. The factors that affect gloss are the refractive index of the material, the angle of incident light and the surface texture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/5d/Gloss_light_Illuminates.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gloss_(optics)","wikidata":"Q900581"},{"title":"Kiss","blocks":[{"text":"A kiss is the touching or pressing of one's lips against another person, animal, or object. The cultural connotations associated with kissing vary significantly between different societies and contexts. Depending on the culture and circumstances, a kiss can express a wide range of emotions, such as love, passion, romance, sexual attraction, sexual arousal, affection, respect, a wish for peace or good luck, as well as numerous other meanings. In some situations, kissing takes on the function of a greeting or a ritual, formal, or symbolic gesture indicating religious devotion, institutional respect, or an act of sacramental nature."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg/330px-Cassatt_Mary_Maternal_Kiss_1896.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kiss","wikidata":"Q7307"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Nanorough.gif/330px-Nanorough.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Nanorough.gif/330px-Nanorough.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Figure1: Specular reflection of light from a rough surface","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANanorough.gif"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Specular_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Specular_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpecular_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Sheen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/da/Sheen.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASheen.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Contrast_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1e/Contrast_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AContrast_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Absence_of_bloom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/10/Absence_of_bloom.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAbsence_of_bloom.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Distinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/3/3b/Distinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistinctness_of_image_gloss.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Gloss-samples.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/15/Gloss-samples.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGloss-samples.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/500px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/USMC-16853.jpg/1280px-USMC-16853.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campa